 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to designating the Battenkill river as an inland waterway for purposes of waterfront revitalization",
    "basePrintNo": "S6333",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6333-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6333\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to\ndesignating the Battenkill river as an inland waterway for purposes of\nwaterfront revitalization\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill adds the Battenkill River to the definition of \"inland\nwaterways\" for purposes of waterfront revitalization.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 -amends paragraph (b) of subdivision 4 of section 911 of the\nexecutive law to add the Battenkill River to the definition of \"inland\nwaterways.\"\n\nSection 2- contains the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill originated as a local request to add the Battenkill River to\nthe definition of \"inland waterways\" to permit the communities in the\narea to apply for grants under the Local Waterfront Revitalization\nProgram and would allow for further competitiveness.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
